1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,778
Unwashed hands killed mothers. His warning was ignored.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:05,326
Vienna General Hospital had two maternity wards.

3
00:00:05,433 --> 00:00:08,284
The first was run by doctors. The second by midwives.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,002
Women in the doctors' ward died of childbed fever far more often.

5
00:00:12,133 --> 00:00:15,732
Ignaz Semmelweis noticed the doctors came straight from autopsies.

6
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:20,523
A colleague cut his finger during an autopsy, and died with the same symptoms as the mothers.

7
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:24,422
So Semmelweis ordered doctors to wash their hands in chlorinated lime.

8
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:26,449
Deaths in the first ward dropped sharply.

9
00:00:26,567 --> 00:00:29,716
Senior doctors were insulted. Many would not accept he was right.

10
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:33,036
He lost his post, and his ideas were ignored for years.

11
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:38,325
In 1865, after an injury became infected, he died in an asylum.

12
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:42,080
Later research, by Pasteur and Lister, explained why he was right.

13
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,804
Wash your hands. A doctor's warning, ignored for decades.
